<% content_for :title, "My Spirituality | Bipolar Sober" %>

<main class="my-spirituality-page">

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="my-spirituality-hero">

    <div class="my-spirituality-hero-content">

      <p class="my-spirituality-eyebrow">
        BIPOLAR SOBER / SPIRITUALITY / MY SPIRITUALITY
      </p>

      <h1>
        <span>I DON'T</span>
        <span>KNOW WHAT</span>
        <span>THE FUCK</span>
        <span>IS OUT THERE.</span>
      </h1>

      <p class="my-spirituality-intro">
        THE UNIVERSE. NATURE. ENERGY.<br>
        MY ANCESTORS. A LITTLE MYSTERY.<br>
        AND A LOT OF QUESTIONS.
      </p>

    </div>

  </section>


  <!-- CONTENT -->
  <section class="my-spirituality-content">


    <!-- 01 -->
    <article class="ms-section ms-section-black">

      <p class="ms-number">01 / WHAT I BELIEVE</p>

      <h2>
        I DON'T NEED<br>
        TO HAVE ALL<br>
        THE ANSWERS.
      </h2>

      <div class="ms-copy">

        <p>
          My spirituality doesn't fit neatly into one religion.
        </p>

        <p>
          I'm interested in Buddhism. I learn from Hinduism.
          There are things in Christianity and other traditions
          that make me think.
        </p>

        <p>
          But underneath all of that is something harder for me
          to put into words.
        </p>

        <p>
          I believe there is something bigger than me.
        </p>

        <p>
          I call it <strong>the universe.</strong>
        </p>

        <p>
          I don't mean I have some perfect definition of what that is.
          I fucking don't.
        </p>

        <div class="ms-callout">
          I DON'T HAVE TO UNDERSTAND<br>
          SOMETHING COMPLETELY<br>
          TO FEEL CONNECTED TO IT.
        </div>

      </div>

    </article>


    <!-- 02 -->
    <article class="ms-section ms-section-pink">

      <p class="ms-number">02 / THE UNIVERSE</p>

      <h2>
        SOMETHING<br>
        BIGGER<br>
        THAN ME.
      </h2>

      <div class="ms-copy">

        <p>
          When I say "the universe," I mean more than planets,
          stars, and everything floating around in space.
        </p>

        <p>
          It's my way of talking about the whole fucking thing:
          nature, the heavens, life, energy, connection,
          whatever exists beyond what I can understand.
        </p>

        <p>
          I don't picture a person sitting somewhere controlling
          every event in my life.
        </p>

        <p>
          It's more like recognizing that I am one tiny piece
          of something unimaginably larger.
        </p>

        <div class="ms-thought">
          I AM PART OF THIS.<br>
          I AM NOT THE CENTER OF IT.
        </div>

        <p>
          Weirdly, I find that comforting.
        </p>

      </div>

    </article>


    <!-- 03 -->
    <article class="ms-section ms-section-yellow">

      <p class="ms-number">03 / NATURE</p>

      <h2>
        THIS IS<br>
        WHERE I<br>
        FEEL IT.
      </h2>

      <div class="ms-copy">

        <p>
          Nature makes spirituality feel less theoretical to me.
        </p>

        <p>
          Mountains. Trees. Animals. Weather. Water.
          The sky changing. Seasons changing.
          Things dying and other things growing.
        </p>

        <p>
          Nature doesn't need me to explain it.
        </p>

        <p>
          It reminds me that change isn't some personal failure.
          Change is built into everything.
        </p>

        <div class="ms-callout">
          I DON'T HAVE TO GO LOOKING<br>
          FOR SOMETHING SACRED<br>
          IN SOME FARAWAY FUCKING PLACE.
        </div>

        <p>
          Sometimes I can just go outside.
        </p>

      </div>

    </article>


    <!-- 04 -->
    <article class="ms-section ms-section-purple">

      <p class="ms-number">04 / MY ANCESTORS</p>

      <h2>
        THE PEOPLE<br>
        I STILL<br>
        CARRY.
      </h2>

      <div class="ms-copy">

        <p>
          I believe the people we love can remain connected to us
          after they're gone.
        </p>

        <p>
          I think about my grandparents as protective presences
          in my life.
        </p>

        <p>
          I don't need to pretend I can prove exactly how that works.
        </p>

        <p>
          It's something I believe and something I experience
          as meaningful.
        </p>

        <p>
          Remembering them reminds me that my life didn't begin
          entirely with me.
        </p>

        <div class="ms-thought">
          I COME FROM PEOPLE.<br>
          I CARRY PEOPLE.<br>
          I REMEMBER PEOPLE.
        </div>

      </div>

    </article>


    <!-- 05 -->
    <article class="ms-section ms-section-black">

      <p class="ms-number">05 / DEER</p>

      <h2>
        SOMETIMES<br>
        A DEER IS<br>
        MORE THAN A DEER.
      </h2>

      <div class="ms-copy">

        <p>
          Deer have become personally meaningful to me.
        </p>

        <p>
          When I encounter one, sometimes I experience it as a reminder
          of my grandparents, the universe, or simply that connection
          I'm always trying to describe and can't quite name.
        </p>

        <p>
          I don't need to declare that every deer is objectively
          carrying a supernatural message.
        </p>

        <p>
          That's not really the point.
        </p>

        <div class="ms-callout">
          THE MOMENT MAKES ME STOP.<br>
          NOTICE.<br>
          REMEMBER.<br>
          FEEL CONNECTED.
        </div>

        <p>
          That's enough for me.
        </p>

      </div>

    </article>


    <!-- 06 -->
    <article class="ms-section ms-section-pink">

      <p class="ms-number">06 / MY ALTAR</p>

      <h2>
        A PLACE<br>
        TO FUCKING<br>
        REMEMBER.
      </h2>

      <div class="ms-copy">

        <p>
          My altar isn't about proving anything.
        </p>

        <p>
          It's a physical place for things that matter to me.
        </p>

        <div class="ms-grid">

          <div class="ms-mini-card">
            <span>01</span>
            <h3>CANDLES</h3>
            <p>
              Light, attention, intention, remembrance.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="ms-mini-card">
            <span>02</span>
            <h3>CRYSTALS</h3>
            <p>
              Objects that carry symbolism and help focus intention.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="ms-mini-card">
            <span>03</span>
            <h3>OFFERINGS</h3>
            <p>
              Food, coffee, flowers, or other gestures of gratitude
              and remembrance.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="ms-mini-card">
            <span>04</span>
            <h3>SOUND</h3>
            <p>
              A singing bowl, silence, music, or anything that marks
              a moment as intentional.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="ms-mini-card">
            <span>05</span>
            <h3>OBJECTS</h3>
            <p>
              Things connected to people, memories, nature,
              or traditions meaningful to me.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="ms-mini-card">
            <span>06</span>
            <h3>GRATITUDE</h3>
            <p>
              The actual fucking point behind most of it.
            </p>
          </div>

        </div>

        <p>
          Ritual gives invisible things somewhere physical to land.
        </p>

      </div>

    </article>


    <!-- 07 -->
    <article class="ms-section ms-section-yellow">

      <p class="ms-number">07 / LEARNING FROM RELIGION</p>

      <h2>
        I CAN LEARN<br>
        WITHOUT<br>
        PRETENDING.
      </h2>

      <div class="ms-copy">

        <p>
          I don't have to call myself Buddhist to learn from Buddhism.
        </p>

        <p>
          I don't have to pretend I understand Hinduism completely
          to be changed by something I read in the
          <em>Bhagavad Gita</em>.
        </p>

        <p>
          I can find wisdom in Christianity without agreeing with
          every Christian belief or institution.
        </p>

        <p>
          I can read Stoicism even though it isn't a religion.
        </p>

        <p>
          The important part is respecting where ideas come from
          instead of grabbing whatever sounds pretty and pretending
          every tradition says the same thing.
        </p>

        <div class="ms-stack">
          <span>LEARN.</span>
          <span>QUESTION.</span>
          <span>RESPECT.</span>
          <span>KEEP WHAT CHANGES YOU.</span>
        </div>

      </div>

    </article>


    <!-- 08 -->
    <article class="ms-section ms-section-purple">

      <p class="ms-number">08 / RECOVERY</p>

      <h2>
        I DON'T HAVE<br>
        TO DO THIS<br>
        ALONE.
      </h2>

      <div class="ms-copy">

        <p>
          Recovery forced me to think about spirituality differently.
        </p>

        <p>
          For me, a Higher Power doesn't have to mean having
          somebody else's exact conception of God.
        </p>

        <p>
          It can begin with admitting something very simple:
        </p>

        <div class="ms-thought">
          MAYBE I AM NOT THE MOST POWERFUL FUCKING THING
          IN THE UNIVERSE.
        </div>

        <p>
          I can ask for help.
          I can listen.
          I can accept that I don't control everything.
          I can belong to something larger than my own immediate
          thoughts and impulses.
        </p>

        <p>
          Spirituality doesn't do my recovery for me.
          I still have to make choices and take responsibility.
        </p>

        <p>
          But it can remind me why those choices matter.
        </p>

      </div>

    </article>


    <!-- 09 -->
    <article class="ms-section ms-section-black">

      <p class="ms-number">09 / MYSTERY</p>

      <h2>
        "I DON'T KNOW"<br>
        IS A PERFECTLY<br>
        GOOD ANSWER.
      </h2>

      <div class="ms-copy">

        <p>
          I don't know exactly what happens after death.
        </p>

        <p>
          I don't know exactly what consciousness is.
        </p>

        <p>
          I don't know whether every meaningful coincidence
          has some cosmic explanation.
        </p>

        <p>
          I don't know exactly what "energy" means beyond the ways
          I experience connection and presence.
        </p>

        <p>
          And I'm okay with that.
        </p>

        <div class="ms-callout">
          WONDER DOESN'T REQUIRE<br>
          FUCKING CERTAINTY.
        </div>

        <p>
          Mystery is allowed to stay mysterious.
        </p>

      </div>

    </article>


    <!-- 10 -->
    <article class="ms-section ms-section-pink">

      <p class="ms-number">10 / WHAT I PRACTICE</p>

      <h2>
        WHAT DOES<br>
        THIS LOOK LIKE<br>
        IN REAL LIFE?
      </h2>

      <div class="ms-copy">

        <div class="ms-practice-grid">

          <div>
            <span>01</span>
            <p>Spend time outside and actually pay attention.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <span>02</span>
            <p>Keep an altar with objects that mean something to me.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <span>03</span>
            <p>Remember and express gratitude for my ancestors.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <span>04</span>
            <p>Read from different spiritual and philosophical traditions.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <span>05</span>
            <p>Use ritual to slow down and make moments intentional.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <span>06</span>
            <p>Notice the moments that make me feel connected.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <span>07</span>
            <p>Ask for help instead of assuming I have to control everything.</p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <span>08</span>
            <p>Leave some fucking room for things I don't understand.</p>
          </div>

        </div>

      </div>

    </article>


    <!-- ENDING -->
    <article class="ms-ending">

      <p>
        I DON'T NEED A PERFECT DEFINITION<br>
        OF THE UNIVERSE TO KNOW I AM PART OF IT.
      </p>

      <h2>
        STAY<br>
        CURIOUS.
      </h2>

      <p class="ms-ending-copy">
        Pay attention. Be grateful. Remember the people you love.
        Keep learning. Leave room for mystery.
      </p>

      <%= link_to "← BACK TO SPIRITUALITY",
          spirituality_path,
          class: "ms-back-link" %>

    </article>

  </section>

</main>